{
 "schema": 1,
 "description": "zerus-a4mub.9 current-read acknowledgement: SharedReadPolicies.current and currentPayload on Android and iOS. target and row are the open conversation; inspection is its verified native inspection; reply_shown is the tail or newest row visible after the settled dwell; attention_shown is its questions (or, without questions, the same tail) visible. current is the parsed authority, payload the mark_read. viewports: SharedReadPolicies.currentShown for one settled viewport. layouts: one settled viewport (offsets and sizes in dp on Android, pt on iOS) mapped by the shared readable-visibility rule (zerus-a4mub.31) to the items it shows (visible), then flags, then currentShown. The rule: an item is shown when the part of it inside the viewport is at least min(its height, readable, the viewport height); the 1-unit history:tail sentinel is shown when it starts inside the viewport and ends at most 2 units past it. Both platforms feed the same shown items to the canonical read dwell and to the current flags.",
